ready: 1
kind: rule
id: consolidation.rule.filing
display_id: RULE-CONSOLIDATION-FILING
module: consolidation
title: What a replayed episode may become
summary: >-
  The episode's emotion label decides which kinds of memory the model may propose from it; anything outside
  that route is refused at validation.
owner: crates/kernle-core/src/consolidation/filing.rs::route
inputs:
- name: label
  source: The episode's appraisal label
  source_kind: stored
- name: explicit request
  source: Whether the episode holds an explicit request to remember, and the kind it asked for
  source_kind: stored
table:
  columns:
  - Label
  - May become
  - Changes allowed
  rows:
  - - Explicit request to remember
    - The kind the request named, else a note or a belief of type fact
    - Add, or update a matching memory
  - - Alarm
    - Guardrail that says what to check before which tools, commands, or paths
    - Add, or update a matching guardrail
  - - Correction
    - >-
      Belief of type preference (the person's way of working), or a guardrail when the correction concerns
      a risky action
    - Add, update, or supersede
  - - Frustration
    - Belief of type learned with the pitfall, the fix, and why, and a lesson on the episode
    - Add, update, or merge
  - - Relief
    - Playbook when a repeatable multi-step procedure succeeded, else a belief of type strategy
    - Add, or update and record a successful use
  - - Surprise
    - Revision of the belief the episode contradicted, or a new belief of type fact
    - Supersede or revise
  - - Approval
    - No new memory
    - Reinforce the belief or playbook that was followed
  - - Curiosity
    - Goal of type exploration for the open question
    - Add, or update the matching goal
  - - Distrust
    - Lower trust in the misleading source
    - Trust assessment change only
  - - Boredom
    - No new memory
    - Reinforce a close existing memory, or nothing
constraints:
- text: Any route may also complete a goal that the episode resolved.
- text: >-
    Values and self-narratives are never filed from one episode; they come only from the belief-to-value
    transition or reflection.
  hard: true
default: Refuse the proposal as outside its route
rationale: |-
  The same experience filed as a generic note would not change behavior at the moment it matters. A near-disaster becomes a pre-action guardrail, a correction becomes how the person likes things done, and a hard-won success becomes a procedure.

  Approval and boredom reinforce instead of creating, because praise and routine success confirm what is already known; a new memory for them would dilute the important ones.
